      <h2 style="margin-top: 3rem;">Cost Comparison by Major Spanish Cities</h2>

      <h3>Madrid (Capital, Highest Cost)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €2,200–€3,200/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €800–€1,200. Rent (outskirts): €600–€800. Madrid is Spain's most expensive city. Strong job market, vibrant nightlife, excellent museums and culture. Public transport excellent (€54.60/month). Dining, entertainment, and social life premium-priced but highly developed.</p>

      <h3>Barcelona (Mediterranean, High Cost)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €2,000–€3,000/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €750–€1,100. Rent (Gràcia district): €650–€950. Beach city with strong tech/startup scene. Slightly cheaper than Madrid but premium compared to other Spanish cities. Beautiful neighborhoods like Gràcia and Sarrià are pricier. Beach culture keeps social life costs down.</p>

      <h3>Valencia (East Coast, Mid-Range)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €1,400–€2,000/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €550–€750. Beautiful Mediterranean city, modern with good nightlife. 30% cheaper than Barcelona. Strong expat community. Excellent public transport. Less touristy than Barcelona or Madrid. Great quality of life at lower cost.</p>

      <h3>Málaga (Costa del Sol, South, Budget-Friendly)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €1,300–€1,900/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €500–€700. Beach town with year-round warm weather. Growing expat community. Lower costs, beach lifestyle. Can feel touristy in summer. Excellent weather year-round.</p>

      <h3>Granada (Andalusia, Budget)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €1,100–€1,700/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €400–€600. Charming university city, very affordable. Strong expat community. Fewer tourists than southern coast. Excellent cultural scene (Alhambra, flamenco). Very cheap living with high quality of life. Growing digital nomad hub.</p>

      <h3>Alicante (Costa Blanca, South, Budget-Friendly)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €1,300–€1,900/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €500–€700. Beautiful beach city. Less touristy than Málaga. Growing expat community, good healthcare, warm weather. Similar cost to Málaga.</p>

      <h3>Seville (South, Historic, Budget)</h3>
      <p>Budget: €1,200–€1,800/month</p>
      <p>Rent (1-bed, center): €450–€650. Largest city in Andalusia. Historic architecture, flamenco, warm climate. Very affordable with strong culture and nightlife. Popular with expats seeking authentic Spanish experience at low cost.</p>

